==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Leaf Cat''' at Level 10.

Evolves into '''Lollycat''' when obtained from [[Panties Awakens!]] (may drop on the first stage but guaranteed on the second) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
This Cat has underwhelming stats, except for the very beginning of the game. Therefore, it is not recommended to use this unit in battle, aside from an assortment of [[Cat Combo]]s. If you really want to unlock it, use them as an extra [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Sexy Legs Cat]].

==='''True Form'''===
Unless aiming at unlocking this unit's Talents, there is no reason to unlock this form, as its DPS, even at level 50, is nowhere near being acceptable for a unit with no abilities and 350 range. It does unlock more combos, though.

==='''Talents'''===
If you are willing to invest NP into them, they become a relatively good [[:Category:Anti-Metal Cats|anti-Metal]] as they have Area Attack and the [[Slow]] ability. Since they have Area Attack and more range, they're generally more effective than [[Clockwork Cat (Rare Cat)|Puppetmaster & Charley]] and [[Volley Cat (Rare Cat)|Curry Cat]] due to their outrageously short recharge time of only 2.2s, though the aforementioned two require no talents to be usable, and Puppetmaster has a longer slow duration while Curry Cat has the ability to deal [[Critical Hit]]s.

All talents beyond the ability to slow Metals are very situational and, in general, not worth getting, especially [[Immune to Weaken|Weaken Immune]], which pretty much requires this Cat to be boosted by levels and talents both offensively and defensively before it can be relevant.

==='''Orb'''===
Their health is pitiful, and they rely primarily on outranging enemies. It is not recommended to use any Effect Orb on them, even Defense Up vs. Metals. A Death Mini-Surge Ability Orb could halt the advances of Metals if Lollycat happens to get pushed into, however.

